     "text": "{\"title\": \"Risks and assumptions\", \"text\": \"The primary risks include go-live occurring on 2027-01-11 before historical signed records are fully migrated, and the final bid document exceeding 20 pages or being uploaded past the deadline [RSK-001, RSK-002]. To address these risks, we would accelerate migration to complete before 2027-01-11, agree with the College to provide access to the legacy archive for historical lookups until migration finishes, enforce a strict 18-page limit during drafting, and upload the proposal 24 hours prior to the deadline [RSK-001, RSK-002]. Managing these risks prevents students and staff from being unable to access prior signed documents during spring enrollment and avoids outright rejection of the proposal without evaluation [RSK-001, RSK-002]. Additionally, it is an open question whether the migration deadline of 2027-02-28 takes precedence over the spring enrollment go-live date of 2027-01-11 for historical records accessibility [Q-01].\", \"cited_ids\": [\"RSK-001\", \"RSK-002\", \"Q-01\"]}",
